{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Seven for your sins.</b> One must ponder: three times it says ״עַל חַטֹּאתֵיכֶם״ ('upon your sins'), and once in between it inserted ״שֶׁבַע כְּחַטֹּאתֵיכֶם״ ('seven like your sins'). And there is also a variation of expression in these four places, and surely they were not incidental. And it appears that at first He said ״שֶׁבַע עַל חַטֹּאתֵיכֶם״ — corresponding to the seven sins that Rashi enumerated, and He said that the punishments would not be aimed measure for measure, because every kind cleaves more to its own kind than to that which is not its kind; therefore HaShem in His compassion did not want the blow to be of the same kind as the sin, so that the blow would not cleave to them powerfully when kind finds kind. But afterward He said: ״If you walk with Me בְּקֶרִי״ and you say that it is surely a chance occurrence for you and not the hand of HaShem that did this — because you see that the blows are not of the same kind as the sin — ״then I will add upon you a blow seven כְּחַטֹּאתֵיכֶם״, aimed measure for measure, so that you may believe that it is not the mule that kills but the sin that kills (Berakhot 33a). ״And if despite these you are not disciplined״ — that you brazenly say in any case that it is chance for you, and it will not avail that I aimed the blows toward your sins — ״then I too will walk with you בְּקֶרִי״, for until now I still did not abandon you to chance events, and I disciplined you Myself as a man disciplines his son; but since all these — El acts twice (Job 33:29) — and it avails not, from now on I will abandon you to קֶרִי, and then the blows will inevitably be ״שֶׁבַע עַל חַטֹּאתֵיכֶם״ and not ״כְּחַטֹּאתֵיכֶם״, because chance, operating without providence, does not aim the blows against the sins, and the number seven likewise is not under providence — only if all seven wandering stars that act through chance bring evils upon you, therefore they will be in the number seven. And what is said ״and I will strike you even I״ — this is not an actual blow in deed, but this blow is figurative, that I will abandon you to the chance events of time, and they will bring evils upon you without compassion, for there is no compassion in chance. But nevertheless the matter is still in doubt, for perhaps chance will bring them good and it is not a definitive thing. Therefore He said: ״And if despite this you do not listen to Me״, and you say in any case that it is chance for you, ״then I will walk with you בַּחֲמַת קֶרִי״ — He added ״בַּחֲמַת״ ('in the fury of'), for I know how to aim the hour when the array is in fierce outpoured wrath, and at that time I will bring it upon you, and then it will bring evils upon you for certain without doubt."], :book :leviticus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:38:53.395947396Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}